## Team Purpose/Mission:
We hope to answer a research question about economic development & electricity acess using analysis and visualization, applying skills we've learned across this semester.
Our intended audience are global development decision-makers, like NGOs (i.e. World Bank, UN).
We intend our product to look and act professional, with a user-friendly interface/graphics and clear understanding of the data.

## Communication Plan & Collaborative Coding:
We plan to communicate through WhatsApp, and have a group to coordinate our communication. 
Direct requests for communication should be responded to within 24 hours (such as direct @s). 
We will meet regularly on Thursdays between 1:25pm and 3:55pm, with addition meetings as necessary scheduled on evenings or weekends. 
For collaborative coding, we will work on local files as much as possible and individual coding files, then copy-pasting into master documents to avoid versioning issues. 
When we meet weekly on Thursdays, we will establish next-steps and specific deliverables for each group member to achieve before the next weekly meeting. These specific deliverables will work towards a schedule that will allow us to meet the deliverable required at the end of the semester.

## Roles & Responsibilities:
Peter is interested in GIS/python and developing a user interface.
Ishaan is interested in using Python, regression modeling, writing.
Henry is interested in data wrangling and using both R & Python.
Yoyo is intested in using R, looking for patterns, statistics.

Responsiblities will be shared throughout the group, with changes week-to-week depending on what is required at each stage of the process. Clear expectations about what each team member will accomplish each week will be established during weekly check-ins, as well as verification of team contributions of the past week. 

