## Operating Norms & Ground Rules:
Decisions will be made through universal consent. 
Files will be well organized. Raw data files will NOT be edited. Group meetings will be used to discuss important decisions - such as how we should segment or clean the data. Decisions consdidered minor or inconsequential are up to each team member. 

## Values & Behaviors:
Respectfulness, Responsibility, Professionalism, Timeliness, Communication.
- Team members will respect each other's boundaries and personhood. 
- Team members will complete their assigned tasks, and communicate if that's not gonna happen.
- Team members will communicate challegnes with each other, including if they think another team member is not contributing enough or is not following THE CHARTER.

## Resources & Constraints:
We can reach out to Mark Jeuland about the data if we have questions that he might be able to answer, and can reach out to the professors of this course with coding questions. 
We will document clearly assumptions that we make, data we chose to leave out, and decision-making criteria to allow the reproducibility of our work.

## Decision-Making Guidelines:
Decisions will be made through universal consent established at weekly group meetings.
If we cannot reach consensus, we will first make every effort to find middle ground that works for eveyrone. If this is not possible, we will consult the guidance of a professor of this course to learn how we can move forward. If a team member wants to do something extra, they can.

## Goals & Objectives:
Something we are proud to show off, which is useful and aesthetic and professional. 
We will meet all the deadlines and expected deliverables of this class.

